# GitHub Workflow Protocol

> Apply when the user asks to "push", "create PR", "verify GitHub", or similar GitHub operations.
> For detailed reference (commands, troubleshooting, branch naming): see `.cursor/docs/github_workflow_reference.md`.

## Pre-Push Checklist

Before committing and pushing, verify:
- All tests pass locally (`make test`)
- Code is formatted (`make format`)
- Linting passes (`make lint`)
- All relevant files are staged (`git status`)

## Commit Rules

- Use conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `refactor:`, `chore:`
- Reference issues: include `fixes #X` or `closes #Y` when applicable
- Keep focused: one logical change per commit

## PR Creation

1. Verify branch is pushed to remote.
2. Create PR via `gh pr create --title "..." --body "..." --base <base-branch>`.
3. PR body must include: summary of changes, related issues, testing notes, breaking changes.

## Post-Push Verification

After pushing or creating a PR:
1. Check CI status: `gh run list --branch <branch-name> --limit 5`
2. Verify test + docs jobs pass.
3. If failures: `gh run view <run-id> --log` for details.

## Summary Report

After completing push/PR/verification, provide a summary:
- Branch pushed successfully (yes/no)
- PR created (if applicable)
- GitHub Actions: test job status
- GitHub Actions: docs job status
- Issues to be closed on merge (if any)
- Any warnings or failures
